{"seconds": 66.2, "exit": 0, "final": "After Qxh7+, Black must play Kxh7 (or Kf6). If Kxh7, then White has likely won the game with a mating attack. This is the line! The move is **Nf7**.\n\n**Best move:** Nf7\n\n**Main line:** Nf7 Kxf7 (forced, or king moves and the bishop stays hanging) Qh5+ Kg7 (Kg8 Qxh7+ Kh8/Kf7 is similar; Ke7 or Kf6 lose the bishop) Qxh7+ Kxh7 and White has a winning attack with the queen and knights.\n\n**Motif:** Attraction (or sacrifice) - White sacrifices the knight to lure the Black king into an exposed position where it becomes mated.\n\n**Explanation (coaching note):**\nYour knight on e5 was perfectly placed to sacrifice on f7, forcing Black's king out. You saw a hanging bishop but missed that after Kxf7, your queen delivers check from h5, attacking the undefended h7 pawn. When the king moves, Qxh7+ shatters Black's kingside defense. Sacrifice the knight to attract the king into danger\u2014this common pattern ends many attacks at club level.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf7\", \"line\": [\"Nf7\", \"Kxf7\", \"Qh5+\", \"Kg7\", \"Qxh7+\", \"Kxh7\"], \"motifs\": [\"attraction\", \"sacrifice\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nxc6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1N1p3/2Pn1pb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K b - - 0 24", "move": "Qxc6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-ins